desc:JigDAW One-Pole Filter

// A worked example for bin/jsfx-import.js: a standard exponential one-pole
// lowpass, proving that state a script assigns in @sample (z0, z1) survives
// from one process() call to the next, the way plugins/_jsfx-runtime's VM
// keeps every variable in its own register rather than resetting it per
// block.

slider1:cutoff=1000<20,20000,1>Cutoff (Hz)

@init
z0 = 0;
z1 = 0;

@slider
a = 1 - exp(-2 * 3.14159265358979 * cutoff / srate);

@sample
z0 = z0 + a * (spl0 - z0);
z1 = z1 + a * (spl1 - z1);
spl0 = z0;
spl1 = z1;
